# Editor
.vscode/

# Claude Code session state. The worktrees directory is per-session scratch and
# must never be committed; settings.json is deliberately shared and stays
# tracked.
#
# '.claude/*' rather than '.claude/': git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so under '.claude/' the negation below silently does nothing and
# even 'git add .claude/settings.json' is refused. Matching the contents
# instead leaves the directory traversable, which is what makes the negation
# work.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
